# 🎫 Help Desk Printer Scenario

## Ticket ID

`INC-6301`

## User

Jennifer – Finance

## Issue

> "I sent a document to the printer, but nothing printed. The document has been sitting there for several minutes."

---

## Information Gathering

Questions to ask:

1. When did the problem start?
2. Which printer are you trying to use?
3. Is the printer powered on?
4. Is the printer showing an error?
5. Can other users print?
6. Is the document stuck in the print queue?
7. Can you print a test page?
8. Has anything recently changed?

---

# Investigation

The following areas should be checked:

```text
Printer Power
      ↓
Printer Connection
      ↓
Printer Selection
      ↓
Printer Status
      ↓
Print Queue
      ↓
Print Spooler
      ↓
Driver
      ↓
Hardware
```

The technician should start with the simplest and least disruptive checks before making larger changes.

---

# Resolution Principle

Do not assume:

> "The printer needs to be reinstalled."

Instead:

```text
Gather Evidence
      ↓
Identify Cause
      ↓
Make Approved Change
      ↓
Test
      ↓
Verify
```

