# 🏢 Practical User GPO Lab

Today's second major hands-on exercise was a **User Configuration Group Policy**.

The lab structure was:

```text
kpatel.test
    ↓
Users
    ↓
Finance
    ↓
jfinance
```

The purpose was to reinforce the concept that a GPO is normally **linked to an OU**, rather than directly attached to a user.

---

# GPO Structure

The model used was:

```text
User
 ↓
OU
 ↓
GPO Link
 ↓
User Configuration
 ↓
Policy Processing
 ↓
User Receives Setting
```

---

# 🧪 GPO Lab – Finance User Settings

## Step 1 – Open Group Policy Management

The Group Policy Management Console was opened using:

```text
Windows + R
```

Then:

```text
gpmc.msc
```

---

# Step 2 – Locate the Finance OU

The Finance OU was located under:

```text
Forest
 ↓
Domains
 ↓
kpatel.test
 ↓
Users
 ↓
Finance
```

---

# Step 3 – Create a New GPO

The Finance OU was selected.

A new GPO was created and linked to the OU.

GPO name:

```text
GPO-Finance-UserSettings
```

---

# Step 4 – Edit the GPO

The GPO was edited and the following path was used:

```text
User Configuration
 ↓
Policies
 ↓
Administrative Templates
 ↓
Control Panel
```

A user-based Control Panel policy was configured.

The exact available policy/item names can vary depending on the Windows administrative templates installed.

---

# Step 5 – Update Group Policy

On the Windows 11 client, the Finance test user was used.

The following command was run:

```cmd
gpupdate /force
```

Purpose:

Forces Windows to refresh Group Policy settings.

---

# Step 6 – Verify Applied GPOs

The following command was used:

```cmd
gpresult /r
```

The output was reviewed under:

```text
USER SETTINGS
```

The objective was to verify that:

```text
GPO-Finance-UserSettings
```

was applied to the user.

---

# Step 7 – Verify With RSOP

The following command was also used:

```cmd
rsop.msc
```

RSOP stands for:

**Resultant Set of Policy**

It can be used to examine the policy settings that resulted after Group Policy processing.

---

# 🧠 Important GPO Concept

A major lesson from today's exercise was:

> **A GPO is linked to an OU; User Configuration settings in that GPO can apply to users in the applicable OU, subject to Group Policy processing and filtering.**

It is better interview wording than simply saying:

> "I applied the GPO to the user."

---

# GPO Verification Commands

## `gpupdate /force`

```cmd
gpupdate /force
```

Purpose:

Refreshes Group Policy.

---

## `gpresult /r`

```cmd
gpresult /r
```

Purpose:

Displays applied Group Policy information for the current user and computer.

---

## `rsop.msc`

```cmd
rsop.msc
```

Purpose:

Displays the resulting policy settings applied to the system/user.

